T* (KASPER BACKPACK - CARRIER FOR WAVESHARE ESP32-S3-TOUCH-LCD-4.3B) Tj
T* (BUILD, WIRING, POWER AND SERVICE NOTES) Tj
T* (================================================================================) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (LINKS) Tj
T* (- Firmware, docs, unit tests, UI simulator:  https://github.com/bckasper3/WaveShare4.3) Tj
T* (- Board outline / mounting-hole dimensions:) Tj
T* (  https://github.com/bckasper3/WaveShare4.3/blob/main/docs/Kasper_Backpack_REV8_dimensions.pdf) Tj
T* (- 3D-printable enclosure + daughterboard mounting:) Tj
T* (  https://cults3d.com/en/3d-model/tool/waveshare-4-3-enclosure-and-daughterboard-mounting) Tj
T* (- 3D-printable stand / bench holder for the Waveshare 4.3":) Tj
T* (  https://cults3d.com/en/3d-model/tool/waveshare-4-3-lcd-screen-holder-developement) Tj
T* (- Video: https://youtu.be/OviTJG7jLCk) Tj
T* (- Waveshare board wiki: https://www.waveshare.com/wiki/ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-4.3B) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (REVISIONS) Tj
T* (- REV-8: built \(2 boards\), tested 2026-11-20..22.) Tj
T* (- REV-9: latest design, not built yet. Drawn before the REV-8 bring-up findings.) Tj
T* (- Desktop case rev A \(wedge, screen tilted 30 deg\) is sized for REV-9.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (DESIGN FILES \(EasyEDA Pro exports\)) Tj
T* (- ProPrj_*.epro2 = whole project. Gerber_*.zip = fabrication.) Tj
T* (- BOM_*.xlsx + PickAndPlace_*.xlsx = JLCPCB assembly \(LCSC part numbers\).) Tj
T* (- 3D_*.step = assembled board model. SCH_*.pdf = schematic. PCB_*.pdf = all layers.) Tj
T* (- FlyingProbeTesting.json inside the Gerber zip is the authoritative pad-to-net map.) Tj
T* (- REV-8: H10/H11 swap was made after the schematic export. Trust the PCB netlist.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* (BATTERY) Tj
T* (- 1S1P Li-ion/LiPo ONLY: 3.7 V nominal, 4.2 V full. JST-PH 2.0 mm lead.) Tj
T* (- Recommended: 2000-3000 mAh flat pouch \(103450 / 104050 size\).) Tj
T* (- Connector U4: PIN 1 = + \(BATT_P\), PIN 2 = GND.) Tj
T* (  Hobby leads are not standardized: CHECK POLARITY WITH A METER.) Tj
T* (  A reversed cell destroys the TP4056 charger.) Tj
T* (- U4 \(battery\) and U7 \(rocker\) are the SAME connector type. Check before plugging in.) Tj
T* (- Use a PROTECTED pack \(PCM, cutoff ~2.5-3.0 V, a few amps\). The board has no) Tj
T* (  over-discharge, over-current or short-circuit protection.) Tj
T* (- Mount on the flat back with zip ties through the slots. Foam pad or Kapton between) Tj
T* (  cell and PCB. Snug, not crushing.) Tj
T* (- Do not store flat: a protected cell left at cutoff for months may refuse to charge.) Tj
T* (- After connecting or reconnecting the battery: switch the rocker ON, then OFF, once.) Tj
