(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* (POWER) Tj
T* (Inputs) Tj
T* (- USB-C 5 V \(front, U8 TUSB320 CC controller\).) Tj
T* (- 12 V barrel jack 5.5 x 2.1 mm \(F1, D1\).) Tj
T* (- 12 V on DB9 pin 9 \(F2, D2\).) Tj
T* (- 12 V inputs: fused, Schottky diode-OR'd, TVS-clamped \(D3\), AP63205 buck \(U1\) to 5V_DC.) Tj
T* (  5V_DC joins USB VBUS on 5V_IN through D4. Reverse polarity is blocked.) Tj
T* (Rails) Tj
T* (- SYS: ~3.0 V \(flat cell\) to ~4.7 V \(external power through D5\).) Tj
T* (- Boost converter \(U9/L3\) makes a steady 5.1 V for the Waveshare in every mode.) Tj
T* (- 3V3_AON: small LDO \(U6\), always on: INA219 + TUSB320.) Tj
T* (Charging) Tj
T* (- TP4056 \(U3\), 600 mA \(set by R13\), CC/CV to 4.20 V.) Tj
T* (- ~4 h for a 2000 mAh cell from empty. Works with the rocker on or off.) Tj
T* (- CHG_EN \(TP4056 CE\) pulled up by R14 = charging enabled by default.) Tj
T* (  Waveshare DO0 ON = charging DISABLED \(firmware uses it for weak USB sources\).) Tj
T* (- From a PC port: 4.71 V at the connector, 4.26 V on 5V_IN \(Q6 + D8 drop\),) Tj
T* (  so the last part of the charge is slow.) Tj
T* (USB host output) Tj
T* (- 5 V to a flash drive, TPS2041B current limit \(~0.5 A continuous\).) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (POWER DRAW \(measured on REV-8 unless noted\)) Tj
T* (- Screen on: ~570 mA from the cell \(~550 mA at 5 V\).) Tj
T* (- Boost input peaks: ~1.4-1.8 A from a 3.4 V cell.) Tj
T* (- Rocker off, standby: ~175 uA \(about 1.3 years on 2000 mAh\).) Tj
T* (- Rocker off right after a battery reconnect: ~800 uA \(about 3-4 months\)) Tj
T* (  until the rocker is switched on and off once \(INA219 powers up in continuous mode,) Tj
T* (  ~0.7 mA; firmware puts it into power-down at every boot\).) Tj
T* (- Standby budget: AP2112K LDO ~55 uA, INA219 power-down ~6 uA, TUSB320 CC watch,) Tj
T* (  diode leakage.) Tj
T* (- Runtime, 2000 mAh, screen at full brightness: ~2.5-3 h \(estimate\).) Tj
T* (  3000 mAh: ~1.5x. Longer with backlight dimming and idle timeout.) Tj
T* (- No battery connected: TP4056 cycles to 4.2 V and back \(LED2 flickers\).) Tj
T* (  Firmware shows battery level as "--" in that case.) Tj
T* (Measuring standby) Tj
T* (- Meter on uA in the battery lead, with a JUMPER ACROSS THE METER.) Tj
T* (- Rocker on ~15 s, rocker off, remove jumper, read.) Tj
T* (- Refit the jumper before touching the rocker or the meter leads. Changing jacks or) Tj
T* (  ranges breaks the circuit, resets the INA219 and reads ~800 uA. It also protects the) Tj
T* (  uA fuse from the 570 mA boot current.) Tj
